WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.619 --> 00:00:02.496
- Good morning Believe Nation it's Evan.

00:00:02.496 --> 00:00:04.941
My one word is believe
and I believe in people

00:00:04.941 --> 00:00:06.833
more than they believe in themselves.

00:00:06.833 --> 00:00:09.403
And my sincere hope is
that if you see in yourself

00:00:09.403 --> 00:00:12.905
what I see in you you'll be
able to change the planet.

00:00:12.905 --> 00:00:15.213
So to help you on your
journey today's message is

00:00:15.213 --> 00:00:17.185
be open to the unknown.

00:00:17.185 --> 00:00:19.185
Over to you Simon Sinek.

00:00:20.297 --> 00:00:21.751
(rooster crowing)

00:00:21.751 --> 00:00:23.993
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:23.993 --> 00:00:27.068
♫ Enspresso keep me goin'

00:00:27.068 --> 00:00:30.005
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:30.005 --> 00:00:31.161
♫ Every morning

00:00:31.161 --> 00:00:33.307
- Rarely are we instant experts.

00:00:33.307 --> 00:00:37.557
You may have a particular gift
or affinity toward something

00:00:37.557 --> 00:00:39.479
but you still get better.

00:00:39.479 --> 00:00:42.463
You know people would pay me
high compliments when I started

00:00:42.463 --> 00:00:45.452
speaking and then people who've
seen me a year or two later

00:00:45.452 --> 00:00:46.974
say that I'm even better.

00:00:46.974 --> 00:00:49.076
And I feel it.
- Why is that?

00:00:49.076 --> 00:00:52.165
- Because you you you learn more you know.

00:00:52.165 --> 00:00:54.678
I think that hubris is
dangerous I think to think

00:00:54.678 --> 00:00:58.202
that you're an expert in
anything is a foolish pursuit.

00:00:58.202 --> 00:01:01.130
You're never you're never
as good as you could be.

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:02.982
There's always room for improvement,

00:01:02.982 --> 00:01:05.423
there's always room to get better.

00:01:05.423 --> 00:01:06.587
You know that doesn't
mean you have to listen

00:01:06.587 --> 00:01:09.240
to all the advice just
you know not necessarily

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.108
because everybody know best.

00:01:11.108 --> 00:01:13.158
But but to believe that you can be better

00:01:13.158 --> 00:01:16.547
and to believe that you can offer more

00:01:16.547 --> 00:01:18.729
is a constant pursuit.

00:01:18.729 --> 00:01:21.039
You know I used to think
being a public speaker

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:23.831
meant being poised and presenting in a way

00:01:23.831 --> 00:01:25.934
that was compelling and
speaking at the right pace.

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:28.853
And that's that's a part of it.

00:01:28.853 --> 00:01:32.352
But but I have been
taking more risks lately,

00:01:32.352 --> 00:01:34.644
doing things that are very unstructured

00:01:34.644 --> 00:01:36.339
and very uncomfortable.

00:01:36.339 --> 00:01:39.623
And I will now do like if
I have an hour to speak

00:01:39.623 --> 00:01:41.405
I'd rather speak for 20 minutes

00:01:41.405 --> 00:01:43.116
and do 40 minutes worth of questions.

00:01:43.116 --> 00:01:44.976
And who knows how that's going to go.

00:01:44.976 --> 00:01:46.451
And that to me, is the best.

00:01:46.451 --> 00:01:48.537
And so I'm a better speaker because now

00:01:48.537 --> 00:01:50.815
I'm way more open to the unknown.

00:01:50.815 --> 00:01:54.446
Where a few years ago that
that would have scared me.

00:01:54.446 --> 00:01:56.638
- One of the greatest
skills I think it can master

00:01:56.638 --> 00:01:59.014
is to learn to be comfortable
and be uncomfortable.

00:01:59.014 --> 00:02:02.235
To lean in on it to feel the
excitement and energy from it

00:02:02.235 --> 00:02:06.385
as opposed to just the
fear and shrinking downness

00:02:06.385 --> 00:02:08.498
is which is what a lot of people do.

00:02:08.498 --> 00:02:11.603
A lot of people are super
uncomfortable when there's a new

00:02:11.603 --> 00:02:14.002
strange scary situation happening

00:02:14.002 --> 00:02:17.113
and want to lean in on that
so you can grow as a human

00:02:17.113 --> 00:02:19.544
but also you can bring
the most to your business.

00:02:19.544 --> 00:02:22.205
A good habit to try to get
into is as soon as you think

00:02:22.205 --> 00:02:24.634
of a new idea, as soon as
you come up with something

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:27.102
that you want to try, you
want to talk to that person,

00:02:27.102 --> 00:02:29.409
you want to launch this
new business, you want to

00:02:29.409 --> 00:02:30.887
create this new campaign.

00:02:30.887 --> 00:02:33.781
Assuming you have that
idea find some small way to

00:02:33.781 --> 00:02:36.004
take immediate action on it.

00:02:36.004 --> 00:02:37.757
One, you're more likely to follow through,

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:39.326
you're more likely to build momentum,

00:02:39.326 --> 00:02:40.917
and to actually see some
results coming from it.

00:02:40.917 --> 00:02:43.576
But two what happens is,
here's what happens so often

00:02:43.576 --> 00:02:45.606
there's so many entrepreneurs
and it's so frustrating,

00:02:45.606 --> 00:02:48.501
it's so limiting for a lot of you guys.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:51.522
Is, you come up with an idea
and you're excited right.

00:02:51.522 --> 00:02:53.414
Like this could be a great
new idea I really want

00:02:53.414 --> 00:02:54.620
to try this thing out.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:57.543
And then you add more
layers and layers and layers

00:02:57.543 --> 00:03:00.505
and extrapolations and
this little tiny idea

00:03:00.505 --> 00:03:03.237
becomes this huge big project.

00:03:03.237 --> 00:03:05.631
And as you scale up the
project and it's exciting

00:03:05.631 --> 00:03:08.547
to think about how you can
make it this big thing right

00:03:08.547 --> 00:03:10.575
if you want to launch a YouTube channel

00:03:10.575 --> 00:03:12.854
it starts with one video
and then you think wow,

00:03:12.854 --> 00:03:14.591
I need to have my banner art,

00:03:14.591 --> 00:03:16.027
I need to have my production schedule.

00:03:16.027 --> 00:03:17.892
I need to figure out what
lights and what camera

00:03:17.892 --> 00:03:18.725
or microphone.

00:03:18.725 --> 00:03:20.471
And you like build up this
huge project that is very

00:03:20.471 --> 00:03:23.091
exciting but then the fear kicks in.

00:03:23.091 --> 00:03:24.718
And then it's like,
well how do I go out and

00:03:24.718 --> 00:03:26.168
accomplish all those things?

00:03:26.168 --> 00:03:27.980
I need a team, I need
money, I need resources,

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:30.989
I need time, I need to plan, I
need to plan, I need to plan.

00:03:30.989 --> 00:03:33.176
And you're stuck in this
constant planning mode

00:03:33.176 --> 00:03:36.436
and it becomes such as
such a big idea but then

00:03:36.436 --> 00:03:38.280
you never do anything about it.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.779
Where if you can cut that
off sooner and as soon as

00:03:40.779 --> 00:03:43.168
you get an idea while it's still little

00:03:43.168 --> 00:03:45.620
of something that you want to try

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.312
go ahead and do it.

00:03:47.312 --> 00:03:49.103
Go and see how it works.

00:03:49.103 --> 00:03:50.161
See if you enjoy it.

00:03:50.161 --> 00:03:51.794
See if you want to do it again.

00:03:51.794 --> 00:03:53.963
I keep thinking back
to dating as an example

00:03:53.963 --> 00:03:56.907
where if you're about to meet
somebody for the first time

00:03:56.907 --> 00:03:58.728
if you're already thinking long term,

00:03:58.728 --> 00:04:00.669
if you're already thinking
about the wedding,

00:04:00.669 --> 00:04:02.752
and the kids, and retirement in depth.

00:04:02.752 --> 00:04:04.605
Like you're thinking all the way out there

00:04:04.605 --> 00:04:06.933
you're putting so much
pressure that you find out

00:04:06.933 --> 00:04:09.342
even going to say hi
to this person and you

00:04:09.342 --> 00:04:11.753
don't even know if it's
ever going to work out.

00:04:11.753 --> 00:04:14.977
Or just go out grab a
coffee, see if you like them.

00:04:14.977 --> 00:04:17.432
See if you want to go up
for another coffee right.

00:04:17.432 --> 00:04:21.500
I think as soon as you
get an idea to just try it

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:23.445
and it's uncomfortable and it's scary

00:04:23.445 --> 00:04:25.867
but just try it in some small way.

00:04:25.867 --> 00:04:28.247
I think about my Malaysia
speech that I did

00:04:28.247 --> 00:04:30.660
a couple years ago it was
a meaningful speech for me

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.960
because the first time I
introduced Your One Word

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.499
and Believe to an audience.

00:04:35.499 --> 00:04:37.408
Maybe I did it to you
guys first on YouTube

00:04:37.408 --> 00:04:39.590
but like to an actual speaking audience.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:43.246
And just before going on
stage I had a woman stop me

00:04:43.246 --> 00:04:45.633
at breakfast and was talking about

00:04:45.633 --> 00:04:48.410
how she was being cyber
bullied and how it was

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:50.351
really impacting her negatively and she

00:04:50.351 --> 00:04:52.781
was thinking of shutting
down all her social accounts.

00:04:52.781 --> 00:04:54.613
And the impact that I had in her family

00:04:54.613 --> 00:04:56.449
and just a really sad story

00:04:56.449 --> 00:04:58.695
from a really beautiful
wonderful caring woman.

00:04:58.695 --> 00:05:01.045
And I was about to get
on stage about to go do

00:05:01.045 --> 00:05:03.872
my second speech and I just
thought of this idea like

00:05:03.872 --> 00:05:06.772
wouldn't it be great
to involve her somehow?

00:05:06.772 --> 00:05:09.379
Wouldn't it be great to get
it give her some recognition

00:05:09.379 --> 00:05:12.045
and have the people in
the audience support her.

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:13.933
And so I brought her up
on stage she had no idea

00:05:13.933 --> 00:05:16.539
what was happening and
I asked her you know,

00:05:16.539 --> 00:05:17.906
"Are you okay if I tell your story?"

00:05:17.906 --> 00:05:19.562
And she said, "Yes." and I told her story.

00:05:19.562 --> 00:05:23.883
And then what I wanted people
to do was while I was speaking

00:05:23.883 --> 00:05:28.050
I had just my new friend
here to the side of the stage

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.393
and I said, "Everybody what
I want you guys to do is

00:05:31.393 --> 00:05:34.644
"come up and take a picture with her,

00:05:34.644 --> 00:05:39.382
"put hashtag I think with
hashtag peace or hashtag love.

00:05:39.382 --> 00:05:41.664
"And anybody who tagged me in
the picture takes a picture

00:05:41.664 --> 00:05:44.020
"with her and has hashtag peace or love,

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:44.853
"I will give them."

00:05:44.853 --> 00:05:47.345
I gave them one of my my guides

00:05:47.345 --> 00:05:48.650
"one of my e-book download that I had.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:51.192
And while I was talking at the front

00:05:51.192 --> 00:05:53.275
there was a huge line up.

00:05:54.205 --> 00:05:57.426
And throughout the entire
presentation people were taking

00:05:57.426 --> 00:06:00.213
pictures with her and they were laughing

00:06:00.213 --> 00:06:02.798
and they were smiling and
there were tears of joy

00:06:02.798 --> 00:06:06.965
and happiness and it really
made an impact on my new friend,

00:06:07.802 --> 00:06:10.230
this woman that I had met,
but also on everybody coming

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:13.611
through that this was something
that was really important.

00:06:13.611 --> 00:06:17.406
And it made the talk that much
more valuable to everybody.

00:06:17.406 --> 00:06:20.436
And it just happened spur the
moment this was not a planned

00:06:20.436 --> 00:06:22.477
thing, if she didn't come
and meet me at breakfast

00:06:22.477 --> 00:06:24.448
and stop me and say hi
and tell me her story

00:06:24.448 --> 00:06:25.638
I wouldn't have done that.

00:06:25.638 --> 00:06:27.918
I would have just continued
with my regular regularly

00:06:27.918 --> 00:06:28.861
planned speech.

00:06:28.861 --> 00:06:31.705
And so I think it's good to
have a plan but it's goof

00:06:31.705 --> 00:06:35.469
to make adjustments, it's
good to lean into the unknown.

00:06:35.469 --> 00:06:39.636
I had this idea and instead
of making it this big thing

00:06:40.929 --> 00:06:43.905
that I could save for the
next time I do a speech,

00:06:43.905 --> 00:06:46.175
or the next time this thing happens

00:06:46.175 --> 00:06:47.609
I'm going to do something right now.

00:06:47.609 --> 00:06:49.520
And it may work and it may not work out

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:51.040
but I'm going to test it.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:53.224
And that one worked out really well.

00:06:53.224 --> 00:06:54.864
But sometimes it doesn't work out right.

00:06:54.864 --> 00:06:56.245
Sometimes you fall on your face.

00:06:56.245 --> 00:06:59.358
Sometimes you think you do
that jump and you can't make it

00:06:59.358 --> 00:07:00.720
and you fall down.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.220
That's going to happen too

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:05.133
but I try to embrace the
approach if I would rather know

00:07:05.133 --> 00:07:07.133
and fail, than not know.

00:07:08.488 --> 00:07:10.477
Then just live in my head

00:07:10.477 --> 00:07:12.972
because I would hate to
think that here is this

00:07:12.972 --> 00:07:15.575
woman who I could have
helped who could have made

00:07:15.575 --> 00:07:17.362
a meaningful contribution to

00:07:17.362 --> 00:07:18.980
and all these people in a
room that I could have helped

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:21.621
them in a meaningful contribution
to but I was too scared

00:07:21.621 --> 00:07:24.662
to do it, I was too scared of releasing an

00:07:24.662 --> 00:07:28.090
imperfect plan and so I did nothing.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:30.244
And that's too often what
we do in our business

00:07:30.244 --> 00:07:31.758
and in our lives.

00:07:31.758 --> 00:07:34.164
We had this idea and we're
too afraid to release

00:07:34.164 --> 00:07:38.164
an imperfect plan and we
do nothing as a result.

00:07:39.206 --> 00:07:41.194
There will never be a perfect plan.

00:07:41.194 --> 00:07:43.521
You can think up a plan
all you want but as soon as

00:07:43.521 --> 00:07:47.344
you start to get out there
into the world and test it

00:07:47.344 --> 00:07:49.437
your plan will change.

00:07:49.437 --> 00:07:51.804
Every single successful
business the plan they started

00:07:51.804 --> 00:07:55.252
with is not the plan that
ultimately helped them grow.

00:07:55.252 --> 00:07:57.998
It was part of their plan,
but they had to change it,

00:07:57.998 --> 00:07:59.170
had to adapt.

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:01.353
And so too many of us are
just stuck in our heads

00:08:01.353 --> 00:08:02.663
and we don't take enough action.

00:08:02.663 --> 00:08:05.012
And so I strongly
encouraged you the next time

00:08:05.012 --> 00:08:07.535
you feel uncomfortable, the
next time you're feeling

00:08:07.535 --> 00:08:09.371
nervous about something,
the next time you get that

00:08:09.371 --> 00:08:11.590
little queasy feeling you know
the, I don't know if I should

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:13.690
do that or not, just do it.

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:14.523
Say yes.

00:08:15.775 --> 00:08:18.712
Embrace the approach it
you would rather know

00:08:18.712 --> 00:08:20.632
and have it fail then live the rest

00:08:20.632 --> 00:08:22.602
of your life with regrets

00:08:22.602 --> 00:08:25.212
because you wrre too afraid
to take some kind of action.

00:08:25.212 --> 00:08:26.881
So the question today is I'm curious

